---
title: "statechart.py: one run of the command"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "The command is alive" as s0 {
    s1: The command starts the janitor process
    s2: The command removes its folders
    s3: The command makes the stage and temp folders
    s4: The command starts the worker, which runs TLC
    s5: The command sends the worker's pid to the janitor
    s6: The command waits for TLC to finish
    s7: The command reads TLC's exit code
    s8: The command moves the chart and report into --out
    s9: The command prints the report to stdout
    [*] --> s1
  }
  s10: The command is dead, and the janitor and TLC may still run
  s11: The command has removed its folders and exited
  [*] --> s0
  s1 --> s2: the janitor process fails to start
  s1 --> s3: the janitor process starts
  s2 --> s11: the folders are gone and the command exits
  s3 --> s4: both folders exist
  s4 --> s2: the worker fails to start
  s4 --> s5: the worker starts and runs TLC
  s5 --> s2: the janitor is gone and cannot get the pid
  s5 --> s6: the janitor gets the worker's pid
  s6 --> s7: TLC exits or the command kills TLC after Ctrl-C
  s7 --> s2: TLC failed (exit 2) or you pressed Ctrl-C (exit 130)
  s7 --> s8: TLC passed or found a bug (exit 0 or 1)
  s8 --> s9: the files are in --out
  s9 --> s2: the report is on stdout
  s0 --> s10: SIGKILL or a crash ends the command
